-DASYSDIC-ULD-STD                  02500+Z0000105830              (new V3.4)                                                   0   - '+E' for the records with BAL def. of object type FILE                0          for additional attributes of object type ELEMENTARY FIELD        0              of DB2 files                                                 0   - '+F' for the records with ADAWAN def. of object type FILE             0   - '+G' for the records with ADASCR def. of object type FILE             0          for the rule coding of object type VERIFICATION (stored in
-DASYSDIC-ULD-STD                  02500+Z0000215710          SYSDIC-DESC)                                                     0   - '+g' for the rule coding of object type VERIFICATION (stored in       0          SYSDIC-VE-ACT)                                                   0   - '+H' for the records with FORTRAN def. of object type FILE            0          for additional attributes of object type DATABASE of             0              type IMS                                                     0   - '+I' for the records with ADAVSAM def. of object type FILE            0          for the description of the IMS/DL1 runtime environment           0              of object type FILE                                          0   - '+J' for the records with C def. of object type FILE                  0          for the records with User profile for PREDICT of object type     0              USER (new V3.2)                                              0          for the records with C def. of object type FILE (new V3.2)       0   - '+K' for the records with User PF-keys for PREDICT of object type     0              USER (new V3.2)                                              0          for the records with ADAINV def. of object type FILE (new V3.2)  0   - '+L' for the records with User profile for LIST XREF of object type   0              USER (new V3.2)                                              0          for the records with SQL create def. of object type FILE         0              (new V3.4)
