-HNSAG-PRD-SYSHELP1                00000+M000000115SYSDIC-ALLDATA
-HNSAG-PRD-SYSHELP1                00000+Z0000007350001PREDICT's generally-applicable help-facility comprises one subroutine   0002that retrieves help information from the data dictionary (SYSHELP1)     0003and 6 help routines that display this help information                  0004(SYSHLP1-SYSHLP6). The library SYSDICH contains all routines.           0005SYSHELP1 is delivered as a load module to guarantee an upward compatible0006interface to PREDICT: you can be sure that your help system will        0007continue to work with the same source code when a new version of PREDICT0008is installed. The helproutines are delivered in source form and should  0009be adapted to the user's requirements.
-HASAG-PRD-SYSHELPA                00000  000000657                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                202012100932546000000000000000PRD851                                           000000000000000
-HASAG-PRD-SYSHELPA                00000  000010688                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                NA                                                              SYSHELPASYSDICH   A0000000000
-HASAG-PRD-SYSHELPA                00000+M000000115SYSDIC-ALLDATA
-HASAG-PRD-SYSHELPA                00000+Z0000015710001Nine parameters can be passed when SYSHELP is called.                   0002                                                                        0003Field-name       FIELDNAME (A32) (INPUT)                                0004                                                                        0005The name of the field for which help information is required. This      0006must be a field of a file defined in the data dictionary,               0007otherwise response-code H'FF' will be received.                         0008                                                                        0009File-name       FILENAME (A32) (INPUT-OUTPUT)                           0010                                                                        0011If the field for which help information is required is not a field      0012of a DDM (userview), it can , for example, be described with other      0013such fields of a special file, whose name can, for example, be          0014the name of the application.                                            0015                                                                        0016If the file-name is the name of a dataview that is defined in a         0017dataarea for a userview, SYSHELP will search via active references      0018for the name of the userview and will substitute that name.             0019                                                                        0020If help information is required for a map, this parameter holds
-HASAG-PRD-SYSHELPA                00000+Z0000105830021the name of the map.                                                    0022                                                                        0023Verification-name         VENAME(A32) (OUTPUT)                          0024                                                                        0025The name of a verification that is linked to the field. If no           0026verification is found, this parameter is blank. Information-type        0027'C' must be called first such that verification-name contains
-HASAG-PRD-SYSHELPA                00000+Z0000215710028either the name of the first verification or blanks. If                 0029information-type 'T', 'V' or 'W' is then specified, response code       0030H'03' indicates that the verification-name contains either the name     0031of the next verification or blanks.                                     0032                                                                        0033Verification-type         VETYPE(A1) (OUTPUT)                           0034                                                                        0035The type of the verification, as follows:                               0036   E - Equal to                                                         0037   G - Greater than                                                     0038   L - Less than                                                        0039   N - Not equal to                                                     0040   R - Range                                                            0041   T - Table                                                            0042   U - User routine                                                     0043                                                                        0044Information-type          INFTYPE (A1) (INPUT)                          0045                                                                        0046The type of information required. The following values can be           0047specified:
-HASAG-PRD-SYSHELPA                00000+Z0000305830048   C - Comments for a field of a file                                   0049   E - Extended description for a field of a file                       0050   P - Comments for a map                                               0051   Q - Extended description for a map                                   0052   V - Comments for an automatic processing rule                        0053   W - Extended description for an automatic processing rule            0054   T - Possible values for a verification
-HASAG-PRD-SYSHELPA                00000+Z0000415710055                                                                        0056Starting-line             STARTLN (N4) (INPUT-OUTPUT)                   0057                                                                        0058The first line of help information to be displayed. If no value is      0059specified , display will start with the first line. After the call      0060has been executed, this parameter contains the number of the next       0061line of help information to be displayed.                               0062                                                                        0063If information-type 'C' or 'E' is called for, responsecode H'03'        0064indicates that starting-line contains the value '1'.  If information-   0065type 'V' is specified and starting-line contains the value '0',         0066SYSHELP searches for the next verification.                             0067                                                                        0068Response-code              RSP (B1) (OUTPUT)                            0069                                                                        0070An indicator for the following error conditions:                        0071                                                                        0072   H'00' - O. K. no error;                                              0073   H'01' - A wrong type has been passed to SYSHELP;                     0074   H'03' - No more information is available for this object;
-HASAG-PRD-SYSHELPA                00000+Z0000505830075   H'04' - No more information of this type is available;               0076   H'FF' - This object is not described in the data dictionary so       0077           no information is available for it.                          0078                                                                        0079Help-Information       HELPINF(A240) (OUTPUT)                           0080                                                                        0081The help information taken from a data dictionary entry. If
-HASAG-PRD-SYSHELPA                00000+Z0000607350082information-type 'C' is specified, this parameter contains up to        0083six lines of comment. If information-type 'E' is specified, this        0084parameter contains up to three lines of extended description.           0085                                                                        0086The help information must be translated into a help screen by the       0087users help routine which calls SYSHELP.                                 0088                                                                        0089                                                                        0090Verification-indicator
